  "title": "Depth is needed: simple abelian sections force rigid selection",
  "subject": "Which Mal'tsev laws can keep a knot inside a globally failing space, and in particular the laws on three values that compose like cycles",
  "conclusion": "In every Mal'tsev law a knot is pulled back from abelian sections of its ranges, so a knot system with declared domains is linear over the abelianized domains, and if every abelian section is simple every global failure on a substrate is rigid. Hence all laws on three values that compose like cycles (all 1020 non-simple ones checked at three places) and all non-affine laws on four values are rigid, while T2(F2) shows two layers are necessary but not sufficient.",
